/E (With k > t+1, the adversary controls t players but needs k shares to sign.Some honest players will contribute shares to signing sessions. Now here's the problem: the simulator needs to generate honest players' shares for signing queries, but the honest players' shares depend on d, which the simulator doesn't know. And the simulator needs to set things up before knowing which message the adversary will eventually try to forge.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
