/P 268 0 R
/T (FROST Assumptions)
/E (FROST Assumptions)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
558 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1102 0 R
/E (Participant Validation: Participants must independently validate the messages before contributing their signature shares to the protocol.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
559 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1103 0 R
/E (Reliable Message Delivery: The protocol assumes that communication occurs over a reliable network channel where messages are successfully delivered between participants and the coordinator.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
560 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1104 0 R
/E (Authenticated Participant Identifiers: Network channels must be properly authenticated to verify the origin of messages, which is strictly required to identify and exclude any misbehaving signers during the protocol.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
561 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1105 0 R
/E (Semi-Trusted Signature Aggregator: A Signature Aggregator \(Coordinator\) is utilized to route messages and coordinate the signing rounds, but it is entirely blind to the private key shares and mathematically cannot forge a signature.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
