575 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1112 0 R
/E (Privacy-Preserving Networks \(Zcash\): Utilizes a custom "Re-Randomized FROST" implementation to allow multiple parties to securely co-manage shielded funds. This ensures that the generated threshold signatures remain entirely unlinkable, preserving the network's strict anonymity guarantees.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
576 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1113 0 R
/E (Decentralized Cross-Chain Exchanges \(Chainflip & THORChain\): Employs FROST to manage massive, globally distributed liquidity vaults \(such as 100-of-150 validator configurations\). This enables rapid, trustless swaps of native assets across different blockchains at a rate of roughly one signature per second.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
577 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1114 0 R
/E (Bitcoin Layer-2 Sidechains \(Blockstream Liquid & Arch Network\): Integrates FROST often wrapped in the ROAST protocol for added network resilience to manage federated sidechains and enable smart contract logic directly on the Bitcoin base layer, drastically lowering transaction fees and data bloat.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
578 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1115 0 R
/E (Next-Generation Hardware Wallets \(Frostsnap\): Powers innovative, open-source multi-signature wallets where several different hardware devices can collaboratively authorize Bitcoin transactions. This reduces on-chain footprint and enhances security against device theft or coercion.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
579 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1116 0 R
/E (Institutional Asset Custody \(e.g., Coinbase\): Replaces legacy, highly complex ECDSA-based multi-party computation protocols. By using FROST, enterprise custodians eliminate the need for vulnerable zero-knowledge proofs, securing billions in institutional digital assets against key-extraction attacks.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
